[{:db/id "f9c73618-b299-5c5a-8259-3519762335fa" :answer/id #uuid "f9c73618-b299-5c5a-8259-3519762335fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 108 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b6677f9e-c46e-5df1-a022-79ff79ead6b6" :answer/id #uuid "b6677f9e-c46e-5df1-a022-79ff79ead6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 216 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e0ded7cd-20cb-515e-90ac-79e2da37e37b" :answer/id #uuid "e0ded7cd-20cb-515e-90ac-79e2da37e37b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5674d226-aed0-5af3-94c0-c08de387fb42" :answer/id #uuid "5674d226-aed0-5af3-94c0-c08de387fb42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 54 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ccb35463-fe83-57c2-9aa8-404bf6c9df5c" :answer/id #uuid "ccb35463-fe83-57c2-9aa8-404bf6c9df5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "108 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fa67956c-515d-580e-8ab9-dbe6238b9841" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa67956c-515d-580e-8ab9-dbe6238b9841" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f9c73618-b299-5c5a-8259-3519762335fa" "b6677f9e-c46e-5df1-a022-79ff79ead6b6" "e0ded7cd-20cb-515e-90ac-79e2da37e37b" "5674d226-aed0-5af3-94c0-c08de387fb42" "ccb35463-fe83-57c2-9aa8-404bf6c9df5c"] :answer-field/correct "f9c73618-b299-5c5a-8259-3519762335fa" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "cb2e2e55-8936-54d7-a33c-03469d398524" :question/id #uuid "cb2e2e55-8936-54d7-a33c-03469d398524" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x^{2} z - 2 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\sin{\\left(t \\right)},3 t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\pi],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, the position vectors of the endpoints of the curve are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨3,0,0⟩ \\\\ r(2 \\pi) & =⟨3,0,6 \\pi⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path defined by $C$ are $(3,0,0)$ and $(3,0,6 \\pi).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r(2 \\pi))-f(r(0)) \\\\  & =f(3,0,6 \\pi)-f(3,0,0) \\\\  & =\\left(- 2 \\left(3\\right)^{2} \\left(6 \\pi\\right) - 2 \\left(3\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\left(0\\right) \\right)}\\right)-\\left(- 2 \\left(3\\right)^{2} \\left(0\\right) - 2 \\left(3\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\left(0\\right) \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =-2\\left(\\left(54 \\pi+0\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =- 108 \\pi.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["fa67956c-515d-580e-8ab9-dbe6238b9841"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8d7fcd3b-6226-5771-b4d1-350798052ab0" :answer/id #uuid "8d7fcd3b-6226-5771-b4d1-350798052ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24 + \\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 50 e^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "15b11761-2ef2-5ceb-a8c8-ffbe832809e5" :answer/id #uuid "15b11761-2ef2-5ceb-a8c8-ffbe832809e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 50 e^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ad9f8939-8a29-5353-a94a-d5c6161080f8" :answer/id #uuid "ad9f8939-8a29-5353-a94a-d5c6161080f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 24 + 50 e^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5550ce8b-a330-5d05-a7e2-450b1c4c0130" :answer/id #uuid "5550ce8b-a330-5d05-a7e2-450b1c4c0130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "888723f5-95e9-5497-a702-b81d6ee6aed4" :answer/id #uuid "888723f5-95e9-5497-a702-b81d6ee6aed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 50 e^{2} - \\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9522aaa5-9e4d-58cf-88b3-a6672f006add" :answer-field/id #uuid "9522aaa5-9e4d-58cf-88b3-a6672f006add" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8d7fcd3b-6226-5771-b4d1-350798052ab0" "15b11761-2ef2-5ceb-a8c8-ffbe832809e5" "ad9f8939-8a29-5353-a94a-d5c6161080f8" "5550ce8b-a330-5d05-a7e2-450b1c4c0130" "888723f5-95e9-5497-a702-b81d6ee6aed4"] :answer-field/correct "8d7fcd3b-6226-5771-b4d1-350798052ab0" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "10952efb-f91e-5efa-8836-2bdfa5e4547d" :question/id #uuid "10952efb-f91e-5efa-8836-2bdfa5e4547d" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} + 2 y z.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨e^{t},t + 3,e^{- t}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, the position vectors of the endpoints of the curve are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ r(2) & =⟨e^{2},5,e^{-2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path defined by $C$ are $(1,3,1)$ and $(e^{2},5,e^{-2}).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r(2))-f(r(0)) \\\\  & =f(e^{2},5,e^{-2})-f(1,3,1) \\\\  & =\\left(2 \\left(e^{2}\\right) \\left(5\\right)^{2} + 2 \\left(5\\right) \\left(e^{-2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(2 \\left(1\\right) \\left(3\\right)^{2} + 2 \\left(3\\right) \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 50 e^{2}\\right)-\\left(24\\right) \\\\  & =-24 + \\frac{10}{e^{2}} + 50 e^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["9522aaa5-9e4d-58cf-88b3-a6672f006add"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8fa93bc4-860e-5e12-a31b-4f116ce4d740" :answer/id #uuid "8fa93bc4-860e-5e12-a31b-4f116ce4d740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 25 e^{2} - 10" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1557e0a8-d585-523d-babf-b225f2b9a2ff" :answer/id #uuid "1557e0a8-d585-523d-babf-b225f2b9a2ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5 - 25 e^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dc7a2ada-2d8c-5325-a3ef-40ae29016e2e" :answer/id #uuid "dc7a2ada-2d8c-5325-a3ef-40ae29016e2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5 + 25 e^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3b9fe5a3-cec7-5200-87f9-a77a6de16f45" :answer/id #uuid "3b9fe5a3-cec7-5200-87f9-a77a6de16f45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 25 e^{2} - 25" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "af665cd1-c2e0-5c16-bd26-b9766458bd3f" :answer/id #uuid "af665cd1-c2e0-5c16-bd26-b9766458bd3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3dbbff86-e68c-5eab-90c3-61a3fcbc667f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbbff86-e68c-5eab-90c3-61a3fcbc667f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8fa93bc4-860e-5e12-a31b-4f116ce4d740" "1557e0a8-d585-523d-babf-b225f2b9a2ff" "dc7a2ada-2d8c-5325-a3ef-40ae29016e2e" "3b9fe5a3-cec7-5200-87f9-a77a6de16f45" "af665cd1-c2e0-5c16-bd26-b9766458bd3f"] :answer-field/correct "1557e0a8-d585-523d-babf-b225f2b9a2ff" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7f288c44-ccaa-54db-bd90-19654202c121" :question/id #uuid "7f288c44-ccaa-54db-bd90-19654202c121" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=- x y^{2} - 2 x y z.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨e^{t},t + 3,e^{- t}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, the position vectors of the endpoints of the curve are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ r(2) & =⟨e^{2},5,e^{-2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path defined by $C$ are $(1,3,1)$ and $(e^{2},5,e^{-2}).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r(2))-f(r(0)) \\\\  & =f(e^{2},5,e^{-2})-f(1,3,1) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\left(e^{2}\\right) \\left(5\\right)^{2} - 2 \\left(e^{2}\\right) \\left(5\\right) \\left(e^{-2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(- \\left(1\\right) \\left(3\\right)^{2} - 2 \\left(1\\right) \\left(3\\right) \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(- 25 e^{2} - 10\\right)-\\left(-15\\right) \\\\  & =5 - 25 e^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["3dbbff86-e68c-5eab-90c3-61a3fcbc667f"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "4a663d34-c8ed-50d1-aa09-4f141042888e" :answer/id #uuid "4a663d34-c8ed-50d1-aa09-4f141042888e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 - 8 e" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "169cc0df-0d15-5b42-b984-d54bb015c91d" :answer/id #uuid "169cc0df-0d15-5b42-b984-d54bb015c91d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1 - 8 e" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "da58d612-7787-54cd-85a7-f3f5f020e812" :answer/id #uuid "da58d612-7787-54cd-85a7-f3f5f020e812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6f6d4e79-214a-5156-9718-c26c48758f6d" :answer/id #uuid "6f6d4e79-214a-5156-9718-c26c48758f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3 + 8 e" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13b122fb-d082-5051-bb26-